# Shell scripts must keep LF endings.
#
# This machine has core.autocrlf=true, which rewrites checked-out files to CRLF.
# A hook checked out that way does not merely misbehave — it never runs: sh
# reads the trailing \r as part of the interpreter path and reports
# "bad interpreter: /bin/sh^M". Pin the endings so the gate survives a checkout.
.githooks/* text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf

# The game collections are data, and their sha256 sums are recorded in
# pgn/MANIFEST.txt. Line-ending conversion would rewrite them on checkout and
# every one of those checksums would stop matching. Keep the bytes untouched.
*.pgn -text
